# The blink goes to the proven PIN_16 header output (Pico rig: GP6 -- or
# clip an LED there); reset comes in on the qualified PIN_10 input (drive
# high to halt, low to run -- Pico rig: GP0). The fabric clock is the hard
# CLKIN, unconstrained.
#
# The board's own LEDs are PIN_25-28 (left-edge IOTILE (0,4)); with SERV in
# the image no placement seed currently routes to that corner of the strict
# conduction graph, so this example uses the header pin until left-edge
# coverage grows.
set_io led   PIN_16
set_io reset PIN_10
